WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
World fertility was 3.31
children per woman in 1990.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.050
By 2024, it was 2.25.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.190
In 1980, China's government began
limiting most couples to one child.

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.830
In 2016, it allowed two.

5
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.050
In 2021, three.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:26.150
And in 2025, it began paying 3,600
yuan a year for each child under three.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.510
Why the U-turn?

8
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.610
Too many people?

9
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.450
A census error?

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.870
Pressure from other countries?

11
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.550
In this mission, you'll
read sex ratios at birth,

12
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.670
and see how Japan is responding
to an ageing population.

13
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.410
Then you'll weigh the evidence
on pro-natalist policy,

14
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.510
from South Korea to a UN review.

15
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:49.210
Your mission: explain China's U-turn,
and judge whether governments can change

16
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.150
how many children people have.
